pokeplatinum-speed-spd2.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the Transitions setting's Platinum side
(docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"; Black's twin: port/extern/lib/gfl/src/fade.c and
port/extern/src/system/game_event.c). Each hook asks port/game/speed_gen4.c, which reads `fadespeed` (0 = the game's, 1 = 2x,
2 = 4x, 3 = Instant). At the default setting each hook is exactly the game's own code path, so the route chain's frames are
unchanged.
Fades: screen_fade.c StartScreenFade (the one entry of every fade: field, menus, apps) halves its framesPerStep, then its steps,
once (2x) or twice (4x), or takes one step of one frame (Instant); both stay >= 1 (the asserts' own bound).
The transition window: field_system.c HandleInputsEventsAndProcesses walks the field task chain (FieldTask->prev) each field
frame and, while a map-change task is in it, opens libntr's SIM_SetTransition window (the game runs at 2x / 4x, its frames are
the same). The tasks are statics of their files, so each file exports a one-line predicate that compares them:
field_map_change.c (ChangeMap, ChangeMapSub, ChangeMapFull, MapChangeFly, MapChangeByFieldWarp, MapChangeWarp: the map changes,
Fly, field warps, scripted map changes), field_transition.c (the fade-out-and-finish-map and start-map-and-fade-in tasks),
unk_02056B30.c (sub_02056CFC: doors, stairs, escalators, warp tiles), pokecenter.c (the healing machine), ov5_021DFB54.c (the
Waterfall climb). Not the new game and continue, the Underground and the Colosseum. The DS build never sees the patch.

field_transition.c also carries Save speed and battle intro's hook (pokeplatinum-speed-spd3.patch: FieldTask_RunEncounterEffect
opens and closes PortSpeed4_EncounterWindow): both insert after EncounterEffectTaskData, so the two are one hunk here.
